      "timestamp_minutes": 55.0,
      "type": "reassess",
      "args": {},
      "justification": "Optional but high priority: Inhalation injury is a major cause of morbidity in burn patients. Assessment for singed nasal hairs, carbonaceous sputum, hoarseness, stridor, or facial burns should be performed to determine if early intubation or bronchoscopy is needed."
    },
    {
